WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.320
Acceptance should produce observable results tied to requirements.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.420
Agree on the configuration, operating conditions and acceptance criteria before testing.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.780
Otherwise, a successful demonstration can become a debate about what success was

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.620
supposed to mean.

5
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.740
The plan may include identity and revision checks, physical inspection, interface verification

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.800
and agreed functional or load tests.

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.040
The exact procedures belong to the qualified teams and supplier documentation.

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.100
This course supplies the review logic, not a substitute commissioning procedure.

9
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.320
Define how exceptions are handled.

10
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:36.220
An accepted deviation needs a scope, technical basis, authorized owner and any

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.120
operating restriction.

12
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.820
A temporary restriction should not vanish when the rack changes hands.

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.900
Preserve the final evidence matrix, accepted configuration and unresolved items in the

14
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:46.640
handover record.

15
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.040
This makes acceptance repeatable and supports later troubleshooting.

16
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.960
It also separates readiness for a limited activity, such as an unpowered

17
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.740
fit check, from readiness for full operation under the required workload and

18
00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:58.540
fault conditions.

